<!--
    The White Noise "M" mark as used by the notification small icon, converted from the
    production logo SVG in the marmot-protocol/whitenoise (Flutter) repo
    (ios/Runner/production.icon/Assets/Logo.svg). The logo geometry is
    unchanged; it is scaled up to span the canvas width with a 52-unit
    (about 1.2dp) margin so it reads at status-bar size. Must stay
    alpha-only white: the system renders small icons from the alpha
    channel and tints them itself.

    Conversation shortcuts use this vector directly, because Android draws
    them well above 24dp. It is also the artwork for the status-bar icon:
    drawable-*dpi/ic_stat_whitenoise.png is rendered from this file by
    NotificationSmallIconBitmapTest. SystemUI draws a vector small icon from
    a cache rounded down to whole pixels, then at a half-pixel offset with
    bilinear filtering, which visibly blurs it; the per-density PNGs keep the
    same artwork sharp.
-->
